    <DataNode elementId="AT2G03760-MONOMER" textLabel="Cytosolic sulfotransferase 12" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P52839" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The ST1 protein is a member of the SULT202 family of sulfotransferases |CITS: [15167709]|. This enzyme can act on a number of brassinosteroids, as well as mammalian hydroxysteroids and estrogens in &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays, but shows a preference for 24-epicathasterone and 6-deoxo-24-epicathasterone |CITS: [17039368]|. Studies using the synthetic substrates (&lt;i&gt;22S&lt;/i&gt;,&lt;i&gt;23S&lt;/i&gt;)-28-homocastasterone and 28-homobrassinolide indicate that the relative orientation of the groups attached at positions 22, 23, and 28 helps to determine substrate preference. The C22-hydroxyl group seems like a likely target for the sulfate addition and the C3 hydroxylgroup has also been mentioned as possible target, but the exact site of modification has not been identified |CITS: [17039368]|. Transcript analyses indicate that the ST1 gene is expressed in the aerial parts of seedlings and that its expression can be up-regulated in response to methyl jasmonate and salicylic acid |CITS: [17039368]|. The biological function of this enzyme has not yet been deduced and sulfated brassinosteorids have not yet been conclusively detected &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; in plants |CITS: [17039368]|. There is some indirect evidence for their existence |CITS: [YOKOTA92]|, but the biological activity of these compounds remains to be determined |CITS: [17039368]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G03760-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G03760.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="P52839" />
